<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>In-depth justification of the hypothesis</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides detailed justifications for the technical assumptions introduced in the main text.
In <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Discussions on ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we analyze the concentration of the smallest eigenvalues
of empirical covariance matrices under mild conditions, thereby establishing <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="H 2 (Model conditionning). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>
for standard random matrix models commonly studied in the literature.
Subsequently, in <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we focus on data augmentation schemes
and identify natural conditions for TDA and GDA under which Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumption5" title="H 5 (Stability of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>
are satisfied.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Discussions on <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="H 2 (Model conditionning). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we establish explicit conditions under which <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="H 2 (Model conditionning). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> holds and provide
closed-form expressions for the parameters <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
These expressions are not directly estimable from data, as they depend on structural properties of the population
covariance <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, in particular its smallest eigenvalue <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Nonetheless, they yield useful theoretical insight into the regimes where our results are applicable.
Formally, we obtain the following result:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="H 1 (Concentration of 𝑋). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and that <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exists a universal constant <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> such that whenever <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<a href="#Thmassumption2" title="H 2 (Model conditionning). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is guarenteed to hold for any choice of <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta&lt;\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}\Bigr),\quad\text{and}\quad c_{X}=c\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{\eta}{\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})}}\Bigr)^{2}\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta&lt;\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}\Bigr),\quad\text{and}\quad c_{X}=c\Bigl(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{\eta}{\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})}}\Bigr)^{2}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To support the previous claim, we introduce a standard non-asymptotic result from random matrix theory.
For a rectangular matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote by <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\min}(\mathbf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\min}(\mathbf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> its smallest singular value.
The following theorem, due to Rudelson and Vershynin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vershynin, 2011</a>, Theorem 5.39)</cite>, provides a sharp lower bound on <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> for random sub-Gaussian matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rudelson–Vershynin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vershynin, 2011</a>, Theorem 5.39)</cite>)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times n</annotation></semantics></math> random matrix with <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq d</annotation></semantics></math>, whose columns are independent, identically distributed, mean-zero, isotropic sub-Gaussian random vectors in <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then there exist absolute constants <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for all <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(s_{\min}(Z)\geq\sqrt{n}-\sqrt{d}-t\right)\;\geq\;1-2e^{-ct^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(s_{\min}(Z)\geq\sqrt{n}-\sqrt{d}-t\right)\;\geq\;1-2e^{-ct^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Observing that <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{-}=\Sigma_{X}^{1/2}Z^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{-}=\Sigma_{X}^{1/2}Z^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> has isotropic and independant columns (under <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="H 1 (Concentration of 𝑋). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and applying <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Rudelson–Vershynin ( , , Theorem 5.39)). ‣ A.1 Discussions on ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> to <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>,
we obtain the following bound on the probability of encountering small
eigenvalues in the leave-one-out covariance matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{X}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{X}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="H 1 (Concentration of 𝑋). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Then, for every <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\leq\eta\right)\;\lesssim\;\exp\!\left(-c\left(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{\eta}{\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})}}\right)^{\!2}n\right)\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≲</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\leq\eta\right)\;\lesssim\;\exp\!\left(-c\left(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{\eta}{\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})}}\right)^{\!2}n\right)\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the same absolute constants as in <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Rudelson–Vershynin ( , , Theorem 5.39)). ‣ A.1 Discussions on ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
In particular, <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ A.1 Discussions on ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> follows directly.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z=\Sigma_{X}^{-1/2}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>X</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\Sigma_{X}^{-1/2}X</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a random matrix with i.i.d. isotropic sub-Gaussian columns, since <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="H 1 (Concentration of 𝑋). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\tfrac{1}{n}ZZ^{\top}\right]=\Sigma_{X}^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}[C_{X}]\,\Sigma_{X}^{-1/2}=\operatorname{I}_{d}\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\tfrac{1}{n}ZZ^{\top}\right]=\Sigma_{X}^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}[C_{X}]\,\Sigma_{X}^{-1/2}=\operatorname{I}_{d}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the inequality <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\min}(AB)\geq s_{\min}(A)s_{\min}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\min}(AB)\geq s_{\min}(A)s_{\min}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})=\tfrac{1}{n}s_{\min}(X^{-})^{2}\;\geq\;\tfrac{1}{n}\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\,s_{\min}(Z^{-})^{2}\;,\quad\text{where}\quad Z^{-}=[Z_{2},\ldots,Z_{n}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})=\tfrac{1}{n}s_{\min}(X^{-})^{2}\;\geq\;\tfrac{1}{n}\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\,s_{\min}(Z^{-})^{2}\;,\quad\text{where}\quad Z^{-}=[Z_{2},\ldots,Z_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, for any <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t\leq\sqrt{n-1}-\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t\leq\sqrt{n-1}-\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\geq\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\,\frac{(\sqrt{n-1}-\sqrt{d}-t)^{2}}{n}\right)\;\geq\;\mathbb{P}\!\left(s_{\min}(Z^{-})\geq\sqrt{n-1}-\sqrt{d}-t\right)\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\geq\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\,\frac{(\sqrt{n-1}-\sqrt{d}-t)^{2}}{n}\right)\;\geq\;\mathbb{P}\!\left(s_{\min}(Z^{-})\geq\sqrt{n-1}-\sqrt{d}-t\right)\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Rudelson–Vershynin ( , , Theorem 5.39)). ‣ A.1 Discussions on ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we deduce that for all <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\geq\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\left(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\tfrac{t}{\sqrt{n}}\right)^{\!2}\right)\;\geq\;1-2\mathrm{e}^{-ct^{2}}\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\geq\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\left(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\tfrac{t}{\sqrt{n}}\right)^{\!2}\right)\;\geq\;1-2\mathrm{e}^{-ct^{2}}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now fix any <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leq\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\bigl(\sqrt{(n-1)/n}-\sqrt{d/n}\bigr)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leq\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})\bigl(\sqrt{(n-1)/n}-\sqrt{d/n}\bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A1.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\eta}=\Biggl(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{\eta}{\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})}}\Biggr)\sqrt{n}\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\eta}=\Biggl(\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{d}{n}}-\sqrt{\tfrac{\eta}{\uplambda_{d}(\Sigma_{X})}}\Biggr)\sqrt{n}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\eta}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\eta}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. And substituting <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=t_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=t_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> into
(<a href="#A1.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.1 Discussions on ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\geq\eta\right)\;\geq\;1-2\mathrm{e}^{-ct_{\eta}^{2}}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\uplambda_{d}(C_{X}^{-})\geq\eta\right)\;\geq\;1-2\mathrm{e}^{-ct_{\eta}^{2}}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is the desired bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Discussions on <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="H 5 (Stability of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we demonstrate that several common data augmentation (DA) schemes satisfy
Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumption5" title="H 5 (Stability of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
We also discuss the limitations of these assumptions and identify scenarios in which they hold exactly,
thereby clarifying the regimes where our results apply.
We begin by introducing a generalization of <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="H 1 (Concentration of 𝑋). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> which will help us achieve more general statements, as well as simplify the proofs.
To this end, we introduce the following definition of Lipschitz concentrated random vectors:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lispchitz concentration)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We say that,</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:15pt;">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The random vector </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is Lispchitz concentrated with parameter </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if and only if for any
</span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-Lipschitz function </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and any </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{f(X_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[f(X_{1})\right]\}\right)\right]\leq\exp\left(\sigma^{2}s^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{f(X_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[f(X_{1})\right]\}\right)\right]\leq\exp\left(\sigma^{2}s^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The probability distribution </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has the Lispchitz concentration property of paramet </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
if and only if for </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is Lipschitz concentrated with parameter </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">and we replace <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="H 1 (Concentration of 𝑋). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> by the following assumption:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption6.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">H 6</span></span><span id="Thmassumption6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lipschitz concentration of the data)<span id="Thmassumption6.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmassumption6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The columns <math id="Thmassumption6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of the data matrix <math id="Thmassumption6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent random vectors,
each of which is Lipschitz concentrated with parameter <math id="Thmassumption6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{X}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{X}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> in the sense of Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Lispchitz concentration). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Equivalently, for every <math id="Thmassumption6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz function <math id="Thmassumption6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="Thmassumption6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\left(s\{f(X_{i})-\mathbb{E}[f(X_{i})]\}\right)\right]\;\leq\;2\exp\!\left(\tfrac{\sigma_{X}^{2}s^{2}}{2}\right),\qquad\text{for all }i\in\{1,\dots,n\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\left(s\{f(X_{i})-\mathbb{E}[f(X_{i})]\}\right)\right]\;\leq\;2\exp\!\left(\tfrac{\sigma_{X}^{2}s^{2}}{2}\right),\qquad\text{for all }i\in\{1,\dots,n\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">One can easily check <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="H 1 (Concentration of 𝑋). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> implies <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="H 6 (Lipschitz concentration of the data). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>,
furthermore the class of matrix satifying <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="H 6 (Lipschitz concentration of the data). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> being stable by Lispchitz transformations (up to a rescaling of a concentration parameter),
will turn out very convenient for the proofs of our main results.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We now provide a set of simple sufficient conditions under which <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is satisfied,
we believe that the vast majority of common data augmentation scheme satify this condition. First, in the case of GDA schemes,
we show that under an almost sure smoothness property of the sample generation process <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> is satisfied:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random matrix.
Assume that for each <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. random vectors with the <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz concentration property,
and where <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,X):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,X):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is almost surely <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.
Then <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=[G_{1},\ldots,G_{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=[G_{1},\ldots,G_{m}]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> of <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>,
with parameter</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{G}\leftarrow\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{G}\leftarrow\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, so that for any measurable set <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathsf{E})=\mathbb{P}(Z\in\mathsf{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathsf{E})=\mathbb{P}(Z\in\mathsf{E})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X)</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional law of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is the pushforward measure of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,X)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{X}=f(\cdot,X)^{\#}\mu\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{X}=f(\cdot,X)^{\#}\mu\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where for a measurable map <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:\mathsf{A}\to\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝖠</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:\mathsf{A}\to\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and a measure <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we recall the notation <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\#}\mu(\mathsf{E})=\mu(\varphi^{-1}(\mathsf{E}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>#</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\#}\mu(\mathsf{E})=\mu(\varphi^{-1}(\mathsf{E}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To show that <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a>, we set <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>
to be any <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz function such that
<math id="A1.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\right]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\right]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider, for <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(sh(G_{1})\right)\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(sh(G_{1})\right)\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(sh(f(Z_{1},X))\right)\mid X\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(sh(f(Z_{1},X))\right)\mid X\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The mapping</span></p>
<table id="A1.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}\;\mapsto\;h\bigl(f(z_{1},X)\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}\;\mapsto\;h\bigl(f(z_{1},X)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">is centered with respect to <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\otimes m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\otimes m}</annotation></semantics></math> by the assumption on <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and it is <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz almost surely,
since it is the composition of a <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz map and an <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz map.
Because <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math> has the <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz concentration property we thus obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(sh(G_{1})\right)\mid X\right]\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\right)\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(sh(G_{1})\right)\mid X\right]\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\right)\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">This establishes that <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> has the <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz concentration property with <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{G}=\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{G}=\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, and completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, in the case of TDA schemes, we have highlight the following sufficient condition for <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> of <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 5</span></span><span id="Thmproposition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random matrix.
Assume that <math id="Thmproposition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X_{I_{j}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X_{I_{j}})</annotation></semantics></math> where:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:15pt;">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-Lipschitz function w.r.t its first argument.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\{1,\ldots,n\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\{1,\ldots,n\})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has the </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-Lipschitz concentration property.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The augmented samples lie in a compact, for all </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z,X_{i})\mid X\right]\|_{2}\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z,X_{i})\mid X\right]\|_{2}\leq K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmproposition5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="Thmproposition5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=[G_{1},\cdots,G_{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=[G_{1},\cdots,G_{m}]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> of
<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for</span></p>
<table id="A1.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{G}^{2}\leftarrow\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}+cK^{2}+c\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{G}^{2}\leftarrow\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}+cK^{2}+c\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a universal constant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that under the assumptions of <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nu_{X}=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(\cdot,X_{i})^{\#}\mu\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nu_{X}=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(\cdot,X_{i})^{\#}\mu\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution of <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(Z\in\mathsf{E}\right)=\mu(\mathsf{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(Z\in\mathsf{E}\right)=\mu(\mathsf{E})</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we used the notation <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\#}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>#</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\#}\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for the pushforward measure, <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\#}\mu(\mathsf{E})=\mu(\varphi^{-1}(\mathsf{E}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mi>#</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\#}\mu(\mathsf{E})=\mu(\varphi^{-1}(\mathsf{E}))</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show that <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> has the Lipschitz concentration property, to this end, let <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Lipschitz function (<math id="A1.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-measureable) such that <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> (note that this can be assumed without loss of generality). For notation simplicity, we further define <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{h}=h-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{h}=h-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have for any <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]\}\right)\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]\}\right)\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\bar{h}(G_{1})\right)\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\bar{h}(G_{1})\right)\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\bar{h}(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\right)\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\bar{h}(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\right)\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Denote by <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}=\mathbb{E}\left[\bar{h}(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}=\mathbb{E}\left[\bar{h}(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, we further write,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]\}\right)\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]\}\right)\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp\left(sm_{i}\right)\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\left\{\bar{h}(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))-m_{i}\right\}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp\left(sm_{i}\right)\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\left\{\bar{h}(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))-m_{i}\right\}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\right)\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp\left(sm_{i}\right)\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\right)\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp\left(sm_{i}\right)\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used the Lipschitz concentration of <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, and the Lipschitz property of <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> in the last bound.
We now denote <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> as the following measure,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\delta_{m_{i}}\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi=\dfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\delta_{m_{i}}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{m_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{m_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Dirac measure at <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Remarking that <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}m_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}m_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> has bounded support (because the <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are boudned and the maps <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> are Lipschitz).
We further write,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]\}\right)\mid X\right]\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\right)\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\exp(s\{M-\mathbb{E}\left[M\right]\})\right]\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[h(G_{1})\mid X\right]\}\right)\mid X\right]\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\right)\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\exp(s\{M-\mathbb{E}\left[M\right]\})\right]\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">to conclude the proof, note that <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math> has bounded support in <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,
as so it is necessarly sub-Gaussian, with sub-Gaussian norm,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|M\|_{\Psi_{2}}\leq\dfrac{1}{\ln(2)}\sup_{i}|m_{i}|\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|M\|_{\Psi_{2}}\leq\dfrac{1}{\ln(2)}\sup_{i}|m_{i}|\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.6.1" class="ltx_text">which follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vershynin (2009)</a></cite>, Example 2.5.8. Thus, we have for a universal constant <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\exp\left(s\left\{M-\mathbb{E}\left[M\right]\right\}\right)\right]\leq\exp\left(cs^{2}\sup_{i}|m_{i}|^{2}\right)\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\exp\left(s\left\{M-\mathbb{E}\left[M\right]\right\}\right)\right]\leq\exp\left(cs^{2}\sup_{i}|m_{i}|^{2}\right)\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.7.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we bound <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math> independantly of <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, leveraging the boundedness of <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. We have,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|m_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|m_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|h(f(0,X_{i}))\right|+\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))-h(f(0,X_{i}))\mid X\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|h(f(0,X_{i}))\right|+\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))-h(f(0,X_{i}))\mid X\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|h(f(0,X_{i}))\right|+\mathtt{L}_{f}\mathbb{E}\left[\|Z_{i}\|_{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|h(f(0,X_{i}))\right|+\mathtt{L}_{f}\mathbb{E}\left[\|Z_{i}\|_{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{i\leq n}\left|h(f(0,X_{i}))\right|+\mathtt{L}_{f}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[Z_{i}^{\top}Z_{i}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{i\leq n}\left|h(f(0,X_{i}))\right|+\mathtt{L}_{f}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[Z_{i}^{\top}Z_{i}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{i}\left|m_{i}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{i}\left|m_{i}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{i}\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]-\mathbb{E}\left[f(G_{1})\mid X\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{i}\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]-\mathbb{E}\left[f(G_{1})\mid X\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\sup_{i}\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\sup_{i}\left|\mathbb{E}\left[h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))\mid X\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left|h(0)\right|+2\sup_{i}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))-h(0)\right|\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left|h(0)\right|+2\sup_{i}\mathbb{E}\left[\left|h(f(Z_{i},X_{i}))-h(0)\right|\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left|h(0)\right|+2\sup_{i}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|f(Z_{i},X_{i})\right\|_{2}\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left|h(0)\right|+2\sup_{i}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|f(Z_{i},X_{i})\right\|_{2}\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left|h(0)\right|+2\sup_{i}\left\|\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z_{i},X_{i})\mid X\right]\right\|_{2}+2\sup_{i}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[\|f(Z_{i},X_{i})-\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z_{i},X_{i})\mid X\right]\|_{2}\mid X\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left|h(0)\right|+2\sup_{i}\left\|\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z_{i},X_{i})\mid X\right]\right\|_{2}+2\sup_{i}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[\|f(Z_{i},X_{i})-\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z_{i},X_{i})\mid X\right]\|_{2}\mid X\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\sup_{i}\left\|\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z_{i},X_{i})\mid X\right]\right\|_{2}+2\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z}\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\sup_{i}\left\|\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z_{i},X_{i})\mid X\right]\right\|_{2}+2\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Where in the last line, we have used the Lipschitz concentration property of <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (as well as <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,X_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,X_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> being <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> Lispchitz), and the fact that <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We conclude the proof by using the boundedness assumption on <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z,X_{i})\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[f(Z,X_{i})\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{i}|m_{i}|^{2}\leq(2K+2\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z})^{2}\leq 4K^{2}+4\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{i}|m_{i}|^{2}\leq(2K+2\mathtt{L}_{f}\sigma_{Z})^{2}\leq 4K^{2}+4\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">plugging this back into (<a href="#A1.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), we obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\left\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[f(G_{1})\mid X\right]\right\}\right)\mid X\right]\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\left\{\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}+cK^{2}+c\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\right\}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\left\{h(G_{1})-\mathbb{E}\left[f(G_{1})\mid X\right]\right\}\right)\mid X\right]\leq\exp\left(s^{2}\left\{\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}+cK^{2}+c\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\sigma_{Z}^{2}\right\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">As consequences of <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Propositions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>,
a broad class of commonly used data-augmentation (DA) schemes satisfy
<a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> from
<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. In particular:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:15pt;">
<li id="A1.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I3.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Deep generative models.</span>
Consider a generative mapping</p>
<table id="A1.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(z,X)\;=\;\theta_{X}^{(L)}\,\sigma_{L}\!\Bigl(\cdots\,\sigma_{1}\!\bigl(\theta_{X}^{(1)}z\bigr)\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi>z</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z,X)\;=\;\theta_{X}^{(L)}\,\sigma_{L}\!\Bigl(\cdots\,\sigma_{1}\!\bigl(\theta_{X}^{(1)}z\bigr)\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the width of layer <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=d_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=d_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{L}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{L}=d</annotation></semantics></math>).
For each <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1,\dots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1,\dots,L</annotation></semantics></math>, assume <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}}\!\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}}\!\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-linear, <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz activation
and <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{X}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}\times d_{\ell-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{X}^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}\times d_{\ell-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a (possibly <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent) weight matrix.
Suppose further that the operator norms are a.s. bounded by a constant <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,
<math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{X}^{(\ell)}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{X}^{(\ell)}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq K</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, by <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the matrix</p>
<table id="A1.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=[G_{1},\dots,G_{m}],\qquad G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X),\quad Z_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\mathrm{I}_{d_{Z}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=[G_{1},\dots,G_{m}],\qquad G_{j}=f(Z_{j},X),\quad Z_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\mathrm{I}_{d_{Z}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">satisfies <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a>.
Indeed, the network <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,X)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\|\theta_{X}^{(\ell)}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\|\theta_{X}^{(\ell)}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz,
hence <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz a.s., from <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> it results that <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a>
of <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with concentration parameter <math id="A1.I3.ix1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I3.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transformative data augmentation.</span>
Likewise, <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> provides mild conditions under which
<a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> holds for transformative DA schemes.
Consider</p>
<table id="A1.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=[G_{1},\dots,G_{m}],\qquad G_{j}=f(X_{I_{j}},Z_{j}),\quad I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\{1,\dots,n\}),\quad Z_{j}\sim\mu\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=[G_{1},\dots,G_{m}],\qquad G_{j}=f(X_{I_{j}},Z_{j}),\quad I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\{1,\dots,n\}),\quad Z_{j}\sim\mu\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">i.e. we randomly select the sample to be deformed, and the deformation is smooth w.r.t. some parameter <math id="A1.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.
Numerous standard transformative DA mechanisms use smooth, small-amplitude perturbations; later in this section we detail the cases of Gaussian noise and random masking.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">The second part <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> of
<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is not always theoretically guaranteed,
yet in the case of an unbiased TDA it is an immediate consequence of the law of total variance.
Indeed, assuming <math id="A1.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}=f(X_{I_{j}},Z_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}=f(X_{I_{j}},Z_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> as in <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and that
<math id="A1.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\,\mathbf{x},\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[f(\mathbf{x},Z)\right]=\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\,\mathbf{x},\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[f(\mathbf{x},Z)\right]=\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can write</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr\}\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr\}^{\top}\,\middle|\,X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr\}\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr\}^{\top}\,\middle|\,X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{X}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-X_{i}\bigr\}\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-X_{i}\bigr\}^{\top}\,\middle|\,X\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{X}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-X_{i}\bigr\}\bigl\{f(X_{i},Z)-X_{i}\bigr\}^{\top}\,\middle|\,X\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\{1,\dots,n\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\{1,\dots,n\})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">In the case of GDA, the decomposition in
<a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> of
<a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> holds trivially, yet no simple expression of
<math id="A1.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{G}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{G}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> exists.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We now spell out conditions under which <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="H 5 (Stability of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> holds. To this end, we introduce the following upper bound:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be two probability measures on <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\!\bigl(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m}\bigr)\;\leq\;\sqrt{m}\,W_{2}(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\!\bigl(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m}\bigr)\;\leq\;\sqrt{m}\,W_{2}(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\!\bigl(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m}\bigr)\;=\;\operatorname{inf}_{\gamma_{m}\in\Gamma(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m})}\int\|x-x^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{m}(x,x^{\prime})\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>inf</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\!\bigl(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m}\bigr)\;=\;\operatorname{inf}_{\gamma_{m}\in\Gamma(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m})}\int\|x-x^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{m}(x,x^{\prime})\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of all couplings and
<math id="A1.SS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Euclidean/Frobenius norm on <math id="A1.SS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{*}\in\Gamma(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{*}\in\Gamma(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal coupling for <math id="A1.SS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{2}(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})^{2}\;=\;\int\|u-v\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}(u,v)\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{2}(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})^{2}\;=\;\int\|u-v\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}(u,v)\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consider <math id="A1.SS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{m}:=\gamma_{*}^{\otimes m}\in\Gamma(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{m}:=\gamma_{*}^{\otimes m}\in\Gamma(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, by the definition of <math id="A1.SS2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and Cauchy–Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\!\bigl(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\!\bigl(\mu_{1}^{\otimes m},\mu_{2}^{\otimes m}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int\|x-x^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}^{\otimes m}(x,x^{\prime})\;\leq\;\Bigl(\int\|x-x^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}^{\otimes m}(x,x^{\prime})\Bigr)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int\|x-x^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}^{\otimes m}(x,x^{\prime})\;\leq\;\Bigl(\int\|x-x^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}^{\otimes m}(x,x^{\prime})\Bigr)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\|x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}(x_{i},x_{i}^{\prime})\Bigr)^{1/2}\;=\;\sqrt{m}\,W_{2}(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{m}\int\|x_{i}-x_{i}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\gamma_{*}(x_{i},x_{i}^{\prime})\Bigr)^{1/2}\;=\;\sqrt{m}\,W_{2}(\mu_{1},\mu_{2})\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p16.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p16.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">The previous result is particularly convenient for demonstrating that <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="H 5 (Stability of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> hold,
which will be done in full detail for all DA scheme presented in <a href="#S3.T1" title="In 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Towards a full justification of <a href="#S3.T1" title="In 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we show that (<a href="#S3.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) holds.
In particular, we establish that the following is true:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{j}=f(X_{I_{j}},Z_{j}),\qquad j=1,\dots,m," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}=f(X_{I_{j}},Z_{j}),\qquad j=1,\dots,m,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},\dots,Z_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},\dots,Z_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. random variables. Further suppose that for each <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[f(X_{i},Z_{1})\mid X_{i}\bigr]=\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i},\qquad\beta\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[f(X_{i},Z_{1})\mid X_{i}\bigr]=\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i},\qquad\beta\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.E84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{G}\mid X\bigr]=\beta\,C_{X}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl(f(X_{i},Z_{1})-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)\bigl(f(X_{i},Z_{1})-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)^{\!\top}\Bigm|X\Bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[C_{G}\mid X\bigr]=\beta\,C_{X}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl(f(X_{i},Z_{1})-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)\bigl(f(X_{i},Z_{1})-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)^{\!\top}\Bigm|X\Bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> of <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> holds.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use the notation</span></p>
<table id="A1.E85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[G\mid X\right]=\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{Z}\!\left[f(X_{1},Z)\mid X\right],\,\dots,\,\mathbb{E}_{Z}\!\left[f(X_{n},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[G\mid X\right]=\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{Z}\!\left[f(X_{1},Z)\mid X\right],\,\dots,\,\mathbb{E}_{Z}\!\left[f(X_{n},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the law of total variance,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[G_{1}G_{1}^{\top}\mid X\right]=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)f(X_{i},Z)^{\top}\mid X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[G_{1}G_{1}^{\top}\mid X\right]=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)f(X_{i},Z)^{\top}\mid X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{\mathbb{E}\left[G\mid X\right]}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr)\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr)^{\!\top}\Bigm|X\Bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{\mathbb{E}\left[G\mid X\right]}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr)\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(X_{i},Z)\mid X\right]\bigr)^{\!\top}\Bigm|X\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\,C_{X}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)^{\!\top}\Bigm|X\Bigr]\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>β</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\,C_{X}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)\bigl(f(X_{i},Z)-\sqrt{\beta}\,X_{i}\bigr)^{\!\top}\Bigm|X\Bigr]\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p18.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p18.3.1" class="ltx_text">which concludes the proof.∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Relying on the above results <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we now justify the results presented in <a href="#S3.T1" title="In 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixed Gaussian GDA:</span>
Consider the Gaussian GDA scheme where, for all <math id="A1.SS2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, for some fixed positive semi-definite matrix <math id="A1.SS2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">We recall from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Louart &amp; Couillet, 2018</a>, Theorem 2.19)</cite> that the standard Gaussian distribution <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{N}(0,\mathrm{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{N}(0,\mathrm{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the 1-Lipschitz concentration property. Moreover, the mapping <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}\mapsto\Lambda^{1/2}\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}\mapsto\Lambda^{1/2}\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz (with respect to the Frobenius norm), which, by the same result, implies that <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz concentrated.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p22.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[G_{1}G_{1}^{\top}\right]=\Lambda\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[G_{1}G_{1}^{\top}\right]=\Lambda\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p22.2" class="ltx_p">which shows that the Gaussian GDA scheme satisfies <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, with <math id="A1.SS2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{G}\leftarrow\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{G}\leftarrow\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{G}\leftarrow\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{G}\leftarrow\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p23.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, note that <math id="A1.SS2.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\mathbf{X}}=\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\mathbf{X}}=\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is constant (i.e., independent of <math id="A1.SS2.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>), and therefore trivially satisfies both <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="H 5 (Stability of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gaussian GDA:</span>
In the more general and realistic case where the covariance matrix of the artificial distribution depends on <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>,
we assume that <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda(X))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz (with respect to the Frobenius norm), and that <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{-1}\leq\uplambda_{d}(\Lambda(\mathbf{X}))\leq\cdots\leq\|\Lambda(X)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{-1}\leq\uplambda_{d}(\Lambda(\mathbf{X}))\leq\cdots\leq\|\Lambda(X)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq K</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.
These assumptions directly ensure that both parts of <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> are satisfied:
indeed <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is guaranteed to be <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz concentrated conditionally on <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> for the same reason as in the fixed Gaussian case, and <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> holds with <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{G}(X)\leftarrow\Lambda(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{G}(X)\leftarrow\Lambda(X)</annotation></semantics></math> by definition.
Similarly, the second part of <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is satisfied by the hypothesis on <math id="A1.SS2.p24.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p25.1" class="ltx_p">To show the first part of <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we use an equivalent “Procrustes” form of
2-Wassertein for zero-mean Gaussians with covariances:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{2}\!\bigl(\nu_{\mathbf{X}},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐘</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{2}\!\bigl(\nu_{\mathbf{X}},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E90.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\min_{U\in\mathcal{O}(d)}\bigl\|\Lambda(X)^{1/2}-\Lambda(Y)^{1/2}U\bigr\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\min_{U\in\mathcal{O}(d)}\bigl\|\Lambda(X)^{1/2}-\Lambda(Y)^{1/2}U\bigr\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{tr}\left(\Lambda(X)+\Lambda(Y)-2(\Lambda(X)^{1/2}\Lambda(Y)\Lambda(X)^{1/2})^{1/2}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{tr}\left(\Lambda(X)+\Lambda(Y)-2(\Lambda(X)^{1/2}\Lambda(Y)\Lambda(X)^{1/2})^{1/2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p25.2" class="ltx_p">which follows by expanding <math id="A1.SS2.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A^{1/2}-B^{1/2}U\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A^{1/2}-B^{1/2}U\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and maximizing
<math id="A1.SS2.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{tr}(A^{1/2}B^{1/2}U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{tr}(A^{1/2}B^{1/2}U)</annotation></semantics></math> over orthogonal <math id="A1.SS2.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> via von Neumann’s trace inequality. This yields</p>
<table id="A1.E92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\nu_{\mathbf{X}},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}})\;\leq\;\|\Lambda(X)^{1/2}-\Lambda(Y)^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐘</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\nu_{\mathbf{X}},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}})\;\leq\;\|\Lambda(X)^{1/2}-\Lambda(Y)^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p26.1" class="ltx_p">To further bound the above <math id="A1.SS2.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> metric, we need to prove that spectral transformations
of large symmetric matrices are Lipschitz. To this end, we introduce the following lemma:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be two symmetric matrices in <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, with respective eigenvalues
<math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}(\mathbf{A})\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}(\mathbf{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}(\mathbf{A})\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}(\mathbf{A})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}(\mathbf{B})\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}(\mathbf{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}(\mathbf{B})\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_{d}(\mathbf{B})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on an interval containing
<math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\uplambda_{d}(\mathbf{A}),\uplambda_{1}(\mathbf{A})]\cup[\uplambda_{d}(\mathbf{B}),\uplambda_{1}(\mathbf{B})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\uplambda_{d}(\mathbf{A}),\uplambda_{1}(\mathbf{A})]\cup[\uplambda_{d}(\mathbf{B}),\uplambda_{1}(\mathbf{B})]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where for any symmetric matrix <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{P}\,\operatorname{diag}(d_{1},\ldots,d_{d})\,\mathbf{P}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{P}\,\operatorname{diag}(d_{1},\ldots,d_{d})\,\mathbf{P}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define
<math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{M})=\mathbf{P}\,\operatorname{diag}\!\bigl(f(d_{1}),\ldots,f(d_{d})\bigr)\,\mathbf{P}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐌</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.736em;" width="1.736em"><mi>diag</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{M})=\mathbf{P}\,\operatorname{diag}\!\bigl(f(d_{1}),\ldots,f(d_{d})\bigr)\,\mathbf{P}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the path <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(t)=\mathbf{B}+t(\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(t)=\mathbf{B}+t(\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that each <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric, and</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\,f\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}t\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\,f\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}t\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p27.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p27.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\int_{0}^{1}\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\,f\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\right\|_{\mathrm{F}}\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{1}\left\|f^{\prime}\!\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\,(\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B})\right\|_{\mathrm{F}}\mathrm{d}t\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\int_{0}^{1}\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\,f\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\right\|_{\mathrm{F}}\mathrm{d}t=\int_{0}^{1}\left\|f^{\prime}\!\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\,(\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B})\right\|_{\mathrm{F}}\mathrm{d}t\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p27.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p27.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}\!\bigl(W(t)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}\!\bigl(W(t)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the (matrix) derivative coming from the spectral calculus.
Since <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on an interval containing the spectrum of each <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A1.SS2.p27.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f^{\prime}\!\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f^{\prime}\!\bigl(W(t)\bigr)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> for a.e. <math id="A1.SS2.p27.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\int_{0}^{1}\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,\mathrm{d}t=\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(\mathbf{A})-f(\mathbf{B})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\int_{0}^{1}\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,\mathrm{d}t=\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p27.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p27.4.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the claim. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p28.1" class="ltx_p">To conclude on the Lispchitz bound, apply <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> to <math id="A1.SS2.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)=\sqrt{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)=\sqrt{t}</annotation></semantics></math> on the spectral interval of <math id="A1.SS2.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that we have <math id="A1.SS2.p28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uplambda_{d}(\Lambda(\cdot))\geq K^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uplambda_{d}(\Lambda(\cdot))\geq K^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS2.p28.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f^{\prime}\|_{\infty}=\sup_{t\geq K^{-1}}\tfrac{1}{2\sqrt{t}}\leq\tfrac{\sqrt{K}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f^{\prime}\|_{\infty}=\sup_{t\geq K^{-1}}\tfrac{1}{2\sqrt{t}}\leq\tfrac{\sqrt{K}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A1.E97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Lambda(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\,\|\Lambda(\mathbf{X})-\Lambda(\mathbf{Y})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{\Lambda}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Lambda(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\,\|\Lambda(\mathbf{X})-\Lambda(\mathbf{Y})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\leq\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{\Lambda}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p28.2" class="ltx_p">Combining the previous with (<a href="#A1.E92" title="Equation 92 ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">92</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A1.E98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\nu_{\mathbf{X}},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}})\leq\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{\Lambda}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐘</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\nu_{\mathbf{X}},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}})\leq\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{\Lambda}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mixture GDA (concise).</span>
We consider a DA scheme that, conditionally on <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, samples from a <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-component mixture with</p>
<table id="A1.E99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}=\Lambda_{I_{j}}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}Z_{j}+m_{I_{j}}(\mathbf{X}),\qquad Z_{j}\sim\mu,\ \ I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\ldots,N\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}=\Lambda_{I_{j}}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}Z_{j}+m_{I_{j}}(\mathbf{X}),\qquad Z_{j}\sim\mu,\ \ I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\ldots,N\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p29.2" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the mixture is centered <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{N}m_{k}(\mathbf{X})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{N}m_{k}(\mathbf{X})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded and isotropic with
<math id="A1.SS2.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[ZZ^{\top}]=\sigma^{2}\operatorname{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[ZZ^{\top}]=\sigma^{2}\operatorname{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>–Lipschitz concentrated and, for every <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS2.p29.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded Lipschitz functions (with constants <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Lambda_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Lambda_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{m_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{m_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Let <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> be the uniform measure on <math id="A1.SS2.p29.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</p>
<table id="A1.E100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathbf{X}}(z,k)=\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}z+m_{k}(\mathbf{X}),\qquad\nu_{\mathbf{X}}=(f_{\mathbf{X}})^{\#}(\mu\otimes u)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathbf{X}}(z,k)=\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}z+m_{k}(\mathbf{X}),\qquad\nu_{\mathbf{X}}=(f_{\mathbf{X}})^{\#}(\mu\otimes u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS2.p30.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Concentration and conditional covariance.</em>
Since <math id="A1.SS2.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\otimes u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\otimes u</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz concentrated and <math id="A1.SS2.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz on
<math id="A1.SS2.p30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Supp}(\mu)\times\{1,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Supp}(\mu)\times\{1,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the pushforward <math id="A1.SS2.p30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz concentrated, so
<a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> holds. Moreover,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[G_{1}G_{1}^{\top}\mid X\right]=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\Big(\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}\mathbb{E}[ZZ^{\top}]\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}+m_{k}(\mathbf{X})m_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{\top}\Big)=:\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[G_{1}G_{1}^{\top}\mid X\right]=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\Big(\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}\mathbb{E}[ZZ^{\top}]\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}+m_{k}(\mathbf{X})m_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{\top}\Big)=:\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p30.2" class="ltx_p">and since <math id="A1.SS2.p30.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p30.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> are Lipschitz and bounded, so is <math id="A1.SS2.p30.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{G}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{G}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>; hence the second part of <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and
<a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> of <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> follow.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS2.p31.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">First part of <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</em>
By Kantorovich–Rubinstein and i.i.d. structure,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\!\big(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐘</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\!\big(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E102.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big\|\big(f_{\mathbf{X}}(Z_{j},I_{j})-f_{\mathbf{Y}}(Z_{j},I_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{m}\Big\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;\sqrt{m}\,\Big(\mathbb{E}\|f_{\mathbf{X}}(Z,I)-f_{\mathbf{Y}}(Z,I)\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐘</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big\|\big(f_{\mathbf{X}}(Z_{j},I_{j})-f_{\mathbf{Y}}(Z_{j},I_{j})\big)_{j=1}^{m}\Big\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;\sqrt{m}\,\Big(\mathbb{E}\|f_{\mathbf{X}}(Z,I)-f_{\mathbf{Y}}(Z,I)\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{m}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\big\|(\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2})Z+(m_{k}(\mathbf{X})-m_{k}(\mathbf{Y}))\big\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{\!1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{m}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}\big\|(\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2})Z+(m_{k}(\mathbf{X})-m_{k}(\mathbf{Y}))\big\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{\!1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{m}\left(\frac{\sigma_{Z}^{2}}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\|\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\|m_{k}(\mathbf{X})-m_{k}(\mathbf{Y})\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{\!1/2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{m}\left(\frac{\sigma_{Z}^{2}}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\|\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\|m_{k}(\mathbf{X})-m_{k}(\mathbf{Y})\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{\!1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p31.2" class="ltx_p">If the spectra of <math id="A1.SS2.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> are uniformly bounded below by <math id="A1.SS2.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then by
<a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS2.p31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)=\sqrt{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)=\sqrt{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\;\|\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;\frac{L_{\Lambda_{k}}\sqrt{K}}{2}\;\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})^{1/2}-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;\frac{\sqrt{K}}{2}\;\|\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{X})-\Lambda_{k}(\mathbf{Y})\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;\frac{L_{\Lambda_{k}}\sqrt{K}}{2}\;\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p31.3" class="ltx_p">and
<math id="A1.SS2.p31.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|m_{k}(\mathbf{X})-m_{k}(\mathbf{Y})\|_{2}\leq L_{m_{k}}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|m_{k}(\mathbf{X})-m_{k}(\mathbf{Y})\|_{2}\leq L_{m_{k}}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus</p>
<table id="A1.E106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\!\big(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m}\big)\;\leq\;\sqrt{m}\,\Bigg(\frac{\sigma_{Z}^{2}K}{4N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}L_{\Lambda_{k}}^{2}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}L_{m_{k}}^{2}\Bigg)^{\!1/2}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐘</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\!\big(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m}\big)\;\leq\;\sqrt{m}\,\Bigg(\frac{\sigma_{Z}^{2}K}{4N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}L_{\Lambda_{k}}^{2}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}L_{m_{k}}^{2}\Bigg)^{\!1/2}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p31.4" class="ltx_p">which proves the first part of <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Stability follows similarly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p32" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixed Gaussian TDA.</span>
Consider the TDA scheme</p>
<table id="A1.E107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}\;=\;X_{I_{j}}\;+\;\Lambda^{1/2}Z_{j},\qquad Z_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\mathrm{I}_{d}),\quad I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\ldots,n\}\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}\;=\;X_{I_{j}}\;+\;\Lambda^{1/2}Z_{j},\qquad Z_{j}\sim\mathrm{N}(0,\mathrm{I}_{d}),\quad I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\ldots,n\}\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p32.2" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> (unbiasedness), we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]\;=\;C_{X}\;+\;\Lambda\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]\;=\;C_{X}\;+\;\Lambda\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p32.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, the augmentation noise law <em id="A1.SS2.p32.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">is fixed</em>:</p>
<table id="A1.E109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\mathbf{X}}\;=\;\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\mathbf{X}}\;=\;\mathrm{N}(0,\Lambda)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p32.4" class="ltx_p">hence it does not depend on <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, and <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="H 5 (Stability of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> are satisfied trivially in this setting.
(Equivalently, since the standard Gaussian is <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz concentrated and the map <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mapsto\Lambda^{1/2}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mapsto\Lambda^{1/2}z</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A1.SS2.p32.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Lambda^{1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz concentrated conditionally on <math id="A1.SS2.p32.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.)</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p33" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random masking TDA.</span>
Consider the augmentation</p>
<table id="A1.E110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{j}\;=\;b_{j}\odot X_{I_{j}},\qquad I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\dots,n\},\;\;b_{j}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(1-\rho)^{\otimes d}\ \text{(i.i.d.)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>(i.i.d.)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{j}\;=\;b_{j}\odot X_{I_{j}},\qquad I_{j}\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\dots,n\},\;\;b_{j}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(1-\rho)^{\otimes d}\ \text{(i.i.d.)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p33.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> denotes elementwise product. Assume <math id="A1.SS2.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X_{i}\|_{2}\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X_{i}\|_{2}\leq K</annotation></semantics></math> a.s.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p34" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS2.p34.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Concentration and conditional covariance.</em>
Writing</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\mathbf{X}}=(f_{\mathbf{X}})^{\#}\!\big(\mathrm{Bernoulli}(1-\rho)^{\otimes d}\otimes\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\dots,n\}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>#</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\mathbf{X}}=(f_{\mathbf{X}})^{\#}\!\big(\mathrm{Bernoulli}(1-\rho)^{\otimes d}\otimes\mathrm{Unif}\{1,\dots,n\}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p34.2" class="ltx_p">with
<math id="A1.SS2.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathbf{X}}(b,i)=b\odot X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathbf{X}}(b,i)=b\odot X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz on the compact domain (with a constant independent of <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> by boundedness of <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>). Hence, by <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz concentrated conditionally on <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <a href="#S3.I1.i1" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> holds.
Moreover, <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS2.p34.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1-\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1-\rho</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A1.E111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]=(1-\rho)C_{X}+\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X}),\qquad\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X})=\rho(1-\rho)\,\operatorname{diag}(C_{\mathbf{X}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝐗</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{G}\mid X\right]=(1-\rho)C_{X}+\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X}),\qquad\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X})=\rho(1-\rho)\,\operatorname{diag}(C_{\mathbf{X}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p34.3" class="ltx_p">so <a href="#S3.I1.i2" title="In H 3 (Concentration of 𝐺). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Item</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> also holds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p35" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS2.p35.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Smoothness.</em>
Since <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{G}(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> is a composition of Lipschitz maps on the bounded set <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-K,K]^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-K,K]^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is Lipschitz; this proves the second part of <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. For the first part, couple <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐘</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m})</annotation></semantics></math> by using the same <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{j},b_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{j},b_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> on both sides. Then</p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\!\big(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mi>𝐘</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\!\big(\nu_{\mathbf{X}}^{\otimes m},\nu_{\mathbf{Y}}^{\otimes m}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E112.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big\|\big(b_{j}\odot X_{I_{j}}-b_{j}\odot Y_{I_{j}}\big)_{j=1}^{m}\Big\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big\|\big(b_{j}\odot X_{I_{j}}-b_{j}\odot Y_{I_{j}}\big)_{j=1}^{m}\Big\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{m}\,\Big(\mathbb{E}\|b_{1}\odot(X_{I_{1}}-Y_{I_{1}})\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{m}\,\Big(\mathbb{E}\|b_{1}\odot(X_{I_{1}}-Y_{I_{1}})\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{m}\,\Big(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\|b_{1}\odot(X_{i}-Y_{i})\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}=\sqrt{m(1-p)}\,\Big(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\|X_{i}-Y_{i}\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{m}\,\Big(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\|b_{1}\odot(X_{i}-Y_{i})\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}=\sqrt{m(1-p)}\,\Big(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\|X_{i}-Y_{i}\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{m(1-p)}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{m(1-p)}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p35.2" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[b_{1,k}^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[b_{1,k}]=1-p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[b_{1,k}^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[b_{1,k}]=1-p</annotation></semantics></math> for each coordinate <math id="A1.SS2.p35.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the first part of <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="H 4 (Smoothness of the artificial distribution). ‣ 3 Precision matrix estimation using generic data augmentation ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Stability follows by the same argument.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides the proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Along the way, we introduce several auxiliary lemmas on concentration for transformations of <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> under
<a href="#Thmassumption6" title="H 6 (Lipschitz concentration of the data). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
<a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> establishes concentration bounds for random variables of the form
<math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz only on a subset <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> (not necessarily on all of
<math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>). We show that the Lipschitz concentration of <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> still yields sharp control of
<math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.
<a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Concentration bounds for random quadratic forms ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> then analyzes quadratic forms
<math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})\,X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})\,X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<a href="#Thmassumption6" title="H 6 (Lipschitz concentration of the data). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. The derivations rely on the Hanson–Wright inequality
(see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Louart &amp; Couillet, 2018</a>, Remark 2.31)</cite>).
Building on these results, <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 A deterministic equivalent for R_𝑋(𝜆), with arbitrarly small regularization parameter ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> derives a deterministic equivalent,
in the spirit of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chouard, 2022</a>, Thm. 6.16)</cite>, under <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="H 2 (Model conditionning). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, which allows regularizations
arbitrarily close to <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, <a href="#A2.SS4" title="B.4 Conclusion on the proof of ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> combines the above ingredients to complete the proof of
<a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, throughout this section we set <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{X}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{X}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we study random variables of the form <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is
Lipschitz only on a subset <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> (and not necessarily on all of
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>). We show that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> still admits sub-Gaussian tails and we
derive a tight upper bound on its sub-Gaussian norm in <a href="#Thmproposition6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with a standard Lipschitz extension lemma (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirszbraun (1934)</a></cite>); for completeness,
we include a short proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathsf{E}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathsf{E}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.E116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\;:=\;\operatorname{inf}_{\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}}\Big\{f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\Big\},\qquad\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>inf</mi><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\;:=\;\operatorname{inf}_{\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}}\Big\{f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\,\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\Big\},\qquad\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(116)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})=f(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})=f(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\in\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\in\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X},\mathbf{X}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X},\mathbf{X}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}^{\prime}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{X}^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}\;\leq\;f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}^{\prime}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{X}^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the infimum over <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math> yields
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\leq\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X}^{\prime})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{X}^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\leq\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X}^{\prime})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{X}^{\prime}\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Swapping <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the reverse inequality, hence <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\in\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\in\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Lipschitz property of <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math> implies
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{X})\leq f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{X})\leq f(\mathbf{Y})+\mathtt{L}_{f}\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|_{\mathrm{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}\in\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking the infimum over
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\geq f(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\geq f(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>, while choosing <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> gives
<math id="A2.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\leq f(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})\leq f(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})=f(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X})=f(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Leveraging <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we now prove the announced concentration bound for
<math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is only Lipschitz on <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 6</span></span><span id="Thmproposition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathsf{E}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝖤</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathsf{E}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz. Assume
<math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{\infty}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{\infty}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="H 6 (Lipschitz concentration of the data). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
Then <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{E}[f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{E}[f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)]</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gaussian with variance proxy</span></p>
<table id="A2.E118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{f,\mathsf{E}}^{2}\;\lesssim\;\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E})^{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\;+\;\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{f,\mathsf{E}}^{2}\;\lesssim\;\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E})^{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\;+\;\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where for <math id="Thmproposition6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(p)\;=\;\sqrt{\frac{1-2p}{2\ln\!\big((1-p)/p\big)}}\,,\qquad\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}\,=\,\sigma\big(\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E})\big)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(p)\;=\;\sqrt{\frac{1-2p}{2\ln\!\big((1-p)/p\big)}}\,,\qquad\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}\,=\,\sigma\big(\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E})\big)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(119)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, extend <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(\tilde{f})=\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(\tilde{f})=\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}|_{\mathsf{E}}=f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}|_{\mathsf{E}}=f</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the clipped map</span></p>
<table id="A2.E120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\mathbf{X})\;=\;\max\!\big\{\min\{\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X}),\,\|f\|_{\infty}\},\,-\|f\|_{\infty}\big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\mathbf{X})\;=\;\max\!\big\{\min\{\tilde{f}(\mathbf{X}),\,\|f\|_{\infty}\},\,-\|f\|_{\infty}\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g\|_{\infty}=\|f\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g\|_{\infty}=\|f\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=f</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A2.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)=g(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)=g(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> a.s. Write</span></p>
<table id="A2.E121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}(X)=g(X)-\mathbb{E}[g(X)],\qquad\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)=\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E}),\qquad p:=\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖤</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}(X)=g(X)-\mathbb{E}[g(X)],\qquad\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)=\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E}),\qquad p:=\mathbb{P}(X\in\mathsf{E}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">A direct decomposition gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E122.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{E}[g(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)]=\underbrace{\bar{g}(X)\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\operatorname{Cov}(g(X),\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X))}_{=:W}+p\,\bar{g}(X)+\mathbb{E}[g(X)]\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{E}[g(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)]=\underbrace{\bar{g}(X)\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\operatorname{Cov}(g(X),\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X))}_{=:W}+p\,\bar{g}(X)+\mathbb{E}[g(X)]\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Hölder with exponents <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,3,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,3,3)</annotation></semantics></math> to the MGF of the sum in (<a href="#A2.E122" title="Equation 122 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">122</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\big\{s(g\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}-\mathbb{E}[g\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}])\big\}\right]\leq\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3sW\}\right]^{\!1/3}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,p\,\bar{g}\}\right]^{\!1/3}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,\mathbb{E}[g]\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}\}\right]^{\!1/3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\big\{s(g\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}-\mathbb{E}[g\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}])\big\}\right]\leq\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3sW\}\right]^{\!1/3}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,p\,\bar{g}\}\right]^{\!1/3}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,\mathbb{E}[g]\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}\}\right]^{\!1/3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Two easy sub-Gaussian factors.</span>
Since <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz concentrated and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, there exists a universal <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.E124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,p\,\bar{g}(X)\}\right]^{\!1/3}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}\,p^{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,p\,\bar{g}(X)\}\right]^{\!1/3}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}\,p^{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is a centered Bernoulli random variable with sub-Gaussian proxy
<math id="A2.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}=\sigma(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}=\sigma(p)</annotation></semantics></math> (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Buldygin &amp; Moskvichov, 2013</a>, Thm. 2.1)</cite>), and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbb{E}[g(X)]|\leq\|f\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbb{E}[g(X)]|\leq\|f\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</p>
<table id="A2.E125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,\mathbb{E}[g]\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)\}\right]^{\!1/3}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\{3s\,\mathbb{E}[g]\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)\}\right]^{\!1/3}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The product term <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gaussian (detailed <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> bound).</span>
We prove that <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\bar{g}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}-\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\bar{g}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}-\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gaussian by exhibiting a scale
<math id="A2.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\exp\{W^{2}/S^{2}\}\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\exp\{W^{2}/S^{2}\}\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W\|_{\psi_{2}}\leq S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, using <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u-v)^{2}\leq 2u^{2}+2v^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u-v)^{2}\leq 2u^{2}+2v^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\bar{g}|\leq|g|+|\mathbb{E}g|\leq 2\|f\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\bar{g}|\leq|g|+|\mathbb{E}g|\leq 2\|f\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{2}\;\leq\;2\,\bar{g}^{2}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}+2\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}\;\leq\;8\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}+2\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 8</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{2}\;\leq\;2\,\bar{g}^{2}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}+2\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}\;\leq\;8\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}+2\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Next, by Cauchy–Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})|\leq\sqrt{\operatorname{Var}(g)}\,\sqrt{\operatorname{Var}(\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})|\leq\sqrt{\operatorname{Var}(g)}\,\sqrt{\operatorname{Var}(\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gaussian with proxy <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lesssim\mathtt{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lesssim\mathtt{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a universal constant <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A2.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}(g)\leq C_{0}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}(g)\leq C_{0}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; also <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}(\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})=p(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}(\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})=p(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.E128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}\;\leq\;C_{0}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}\;\leq\;C_{0}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(128)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and set</span></p>
<table id="A2.E129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}\;:=\;\frac{8\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}{\alpha}\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad\frac{8\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}}{S^{2}}=\frac{\alpha}{\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}\;:=\;\frac{8\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}{\alpha}\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad\frac{8\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}}{S^{2}}=\frac{\alpha}{\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(129)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#A2.E126" title="Equation 126 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">126</span></a>)–(<a href="#A2.E129" title="Equation 129 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">129</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{W^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{W^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{8\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}}{S^{2}}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}\Big\}\,\exp\!\Big\{\frac{2\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{8\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}}{S^{2}}\,\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}\Big\}\,\exp\!\Big\{\frac{2\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,\frac{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}}{\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}\,\exp\!\Big\{\frac{\alpha\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}}{4\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,\frac{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}}{\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}\,\exp\!\Big\{\frac{\alpha\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}}{4\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(130)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of the <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm of <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\exp\{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}/\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\}\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\exp\{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}/\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\}\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, Lyapunov’s inequality gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,\frac{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}}{\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}\leq\big(\mathbb{E}\exp\{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}/\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\}\big)^{\alpha}\leq 2^{\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mn>𝟙</mn><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝖤</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,\frac{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}}{\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}\leq\big(\mathbb{E}\exp\{\bar{\mathbbm{1}}_{\mathsf{E}}^{\,2}/\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\}\big)^{\alpha}\leq 2^{\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(131)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#A2.E128" title="Equation 128 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">128</span></a>) in the second factor of (<a href="#A2.E130" title="Equation 130 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">130</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.E132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\!\Big\{\frac{\alpha\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}}{4\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}\leq\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,C_{1}\,\frac{\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p)}{\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\!\Big\{\frac{\alpha\,\operatorname{Cov}(g,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}})^{2}}{4\,\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}\leq\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,C_{1}\,\frac{\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p)}{\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(132)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">for some absolute <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A2.E130" title="Equation 130 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">130</span></a>)–(<a href="#A2.E132" title="Equation 132 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">132</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{W^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}\leq 2^{\alpha}\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,A\Big\},\qquad A:=C_{1}\,\frac{\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p)}{\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{W^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}\leq 2^{\alpha}\exp\!\Big\{\alpha\,A\Big\},\qquad A:=C_{1}\,\frac{\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p)}{\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(133)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Choose</span></p>
<table id="A2.E134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\star}\;:=\;\Big(1+\frac{A}{\ln 2}\Big)^{-1}\in(0,1]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\star}\;:=\;\Big(1+\frac{A}{\ln 2}\Big)^{-1}\in(0,1],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(134)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">so that <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{\alpha^{\star}}\exp\{\alpha^{\star}A\}\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{\alpha^{\star}}\exp\{\alpha^{\star}A\}\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as in (<a href="#A2.E129" title="Equation 129 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">129</span></a>) at <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.E135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{W^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}\leq 2,\qquad\text{hence}\qquad\|W\|_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\;\leq\;S^{2}\;\leq\;C\Big(\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}+\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p)\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>hence</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\exp\!\Big\{\frac{W^{2}}{S^{2}}\Big\}\leq 2,\qquad\text{hence}\qquad\|W\|_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\;\leq\;S^{2}\;\leq\;C\Big(\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}+\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(135)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">for a universal constant <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> (use <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\alpha^{\star}=1+A/\ln 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\alpha^{\star}=1+A/\ln 2</annotation></semantics></math> and the definition of <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>).
By the standard sub-Gaussian MGF bound, there exists a universal <math id="A2.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A2.E136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\{3sW\}\right]^{\!1/3}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}\,\|W\|_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}(\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}+\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p))\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\{3sW\}\right]^{\!1/3}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}\,\|W\|_{\psi_{2}}^{2}\}\leq\exp\!\{c\,s^{2}(\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}+\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}\,p(1-p))\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(136)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Conclusion.</span>
Combining (<a href="#A2.E123" title="Equation 123 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">123</span></a>), (<a href="#A2.E124" title="Equation 124 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">124</span></a>), (<a href="#A2.E125" title="Equation 125 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">125</span></a>), and (<a href="#A2.E136" title="Equation 136 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Some sub Gaussian concentration bounds ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">136</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A2.E137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\big\{s\big(f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{E}[f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)]\big)\big\}\right]\leq\exp\!\left\{c\,s^{2}\Big(p^{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}+\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\Big)\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mi>𝖤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝖤</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\big\{s\big(f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)-\mathbb{E}[f(X)\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{E}}(X)]\big)\big\}\right]\leq\exp\!\left\{c\,s^{2}\Big(p^{2}\,\mathtt{L}_{f}^{2}+\|f\|_{\infty}^{2}\,\sigma_{\mathsf{E}}^{2}\Big)\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(137)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p">for a universal constant <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the desired sub-Gaussian MGF bound and proves the claimed variance proxy.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Concentration bounds for random quadratic forms</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now study the concentration of random quadratic forms of the type <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such quantities naturally appear in the proof of
<a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We prove the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="H 6 (Lipschitz concentration of the data). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Then there exists a universal constant <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\right)\leq\frac{2}{c}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}+\frac{2}{c}\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-})\big)\right)\;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\right)\leq\frac{2}{c}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}+\frac{2}{c}\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-})\big)\right)\;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(138)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the law of total variance applied to <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},X^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},X^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E139.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\mathbb{E}\!\left[X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\mathbb{E}\!\left[X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(139)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-})\big)\right)\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-})\big)\right)\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(140)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we used <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\mid X^{-}]=\operatorname{tr}(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\mid X^{-}]=\operatorname{tr}(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to control the first term. Conditionally on <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Hanson–Wright inequality (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Louart &amp; Couillet, 2018</a>, Remark 2.31)</cite>) yields, almost surely,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left(\left|X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}-\operatorname{tr}\!\big(M(X^{-})\Sigma_{X}\big)\right|\geq t\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-c\min\!\left(\frac{t^{2}}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}},\,\frac{t}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}}\right)\right)\!." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo>)</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left(\left|X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}-\operatorname{tr}\!\big(M(X^{-})\Sigma_{X}\big)\right|\geq t\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-c\min\!\left(\frac{t^{2}}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}},\,\frac{t}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}}\right)\right)\!.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(141)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Writing the conditional variance in integral form,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E142.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\!\left(\left|X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}-\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-})\big)\right|\geq\sqrt{t}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\,\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\!\left(\left|X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}-\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M(X^{-})\big)\right|\geq\sqrt{t}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\,\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(142)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\!\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\!\left(-c\,\frac{t}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}}\right)\mathrm{d}t+2\!\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\!\left(-c\,\frac{\sqrt{t}}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}}\right)\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\!\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\!\left(-c\,\frac{t}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}}\right)\mathrm{d}t+2\!\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\!\left(-c\,\frac{\sqrt{t}}{\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}}\right)\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(143)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}}{c}+\frac{4\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}}{c^{2}}\;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}}{c}+\frac{4\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}}{c^{2}}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(144)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the change of variables <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=c\sqrt{t}/\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=c\sqrt{t}/\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the second integral. Taking expectations in <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\right]\leq\frac{2}{c}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}+\frac{2}{c}\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\right]\!," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo>]</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M(X^{-})X_{1}\,\middle|\,X^{-}\right)\right]\leq\frac{2}{c}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}+\frac{2}{c}\|M(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\right]\!,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(145)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">which, combined with the total-variance decomposition above, completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In the special case where the map <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz on <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="H 2 (Model conditionning). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ B.2 Concentration bounds for random quadratic forms ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> yields:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7</span></span><span id="Thmproposition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <a href="#Thmassumption6" title="H 6 (Lipschitz concentration of the data). ‣ A.2 Discussions on , , ‣ Appendix A In-depth justification of the hypothesis ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="H 2 (Model conditionning). ‣ 2 Inverse covariance estimation using shrinkage method ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. For any functions <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1}:\mathsf{A}_{\eta}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1}:\mathsf{A}_{\eta}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2}:\mathsf{A}_{\eta}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2}:\mathsf{A}_{\eta}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> that are respectively <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{L}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{L}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz and bounded, and any <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{B}\|_{\mathrm{F}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)\lesssim d\,\|\Sigma_{X}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\left\{\mathtt{L}_{1}^{2}+\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\,(1+c_{X}^{-1})\right\}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)\lesssim d\,\|\Sigma_{X}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\left\{\mathtt{L}_{1}^{2}+\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\,(1+c_{X}^{-1})\right\}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(146)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})\mathbf{B}\,X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)\lesssim\|\Sigma_{X}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\left\{\mathtt{L}_{1}^{2}+\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\,(1+c_{X}^{-1})\right\}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})\mathbf{B}\,X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)\lesssim\|\Sigma_{X}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\left\{\mathtt{L}_{1}^{2}+\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\,(1+c_{X}^{-1})\right\}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(147)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.E148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})\mathbf{B}\,M_{2}(X^{-})X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)\lesssim\|\Sigma_{X}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\!\left\{\big(\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}\mathtt{L}_{2}+\|M_{2}\|_{\infty}\mathtt{L}_{1}\big)^{2}+\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|M_{2}\|_{\infty}^{2}\,(1+c_{X}^{-1})\right\}\;," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝙻</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})\mathbf{B}\,M_{2}(X^{-})X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)\lesssim\|\Sigma_{X}\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\!\left\{\big(\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}\mathtt{L}_{2}+\|M_{2}\|_{\infty}\mathtt{L}_{1}\big)^{2}+\|M_{1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|M_{2}\|_{\infty}^{2}\,(1+c_{X}^{-1})\right\}\;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(148)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M_{i}\|_{\infty}=\big\|\|M_{i}(\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\big\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M_{i}\|_{\infty}=\big\|\|M_{i}(\cdot)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\big\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We treat the three cases in the same way. By <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ B.2 Concentration bounds for random quadratic forms ‣ Appendix B Proof of ‣ Non-Asymptotic Analysis Of Data Augmentation For Precision Matrix Estimation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and since <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(X^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(X^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>-measurable,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}\!\left(X_{1}^{\top}M_{1}(X^{-})X_{1}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(149)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{2}{c}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|M_{1}(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)+\frac{2}{c}\|M_{1}(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M_{1}(X^{-})\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\big)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><msub><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{2}{c}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|M_{1}(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)+\frac{2}{c}\|M_{1}(X^{-})\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2}\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\right]+\operatorname{Var}\!\left(\operatorname{tr}\!\big(\Sigma_{X}M_{1}(X^{-})\,\mathbbm{1}_{\mathsf{A}_{\eta}}(X)\big)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(150)</span></td></tr></tbody>
